{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/26252-question-about-mortal-remains-and-god-machine","id":26252,"title":"Question about Mortal Remains and God Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-08T20:19:18-08:00","id":26252,"title":"Question about Mortal Remains and God Machine","content":"From what I have read in the previews, it looks like the upcoming book Hunter: Mortal Remains will also have the necessary information to pull a Hunter game into the post God Machine rules set.<br /> <br /> My question is, will the new material presented in this book be only compatible for Post GMC or will it be in the classic format and you use the rules to pull it into GMC. The reason I ask this question is that I am not a big fan of the GMC rules update and I would enjoy this book a lot more if I dont have to reverse engineer the new material to use it with my non-GMC WOD. The acronyms!!!<br /> <br /> Anyone have any incite to this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If people were meant to run around naked, they would be born that way.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1286-nikuchan","name":"Nikuchan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T20:46:01-08:00","id":26266,"title":"","content":"There's not much to reverse-engineer, really. I can't see there being any hang-ups. Merits and Endowments still work the way they did before, and I can't imagine too many mechanics being hard tied in to Conditions.<br /> <br /> No need to worry, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T17:18:18-08:00","id":32846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nikuchan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/26252-question-about-mortal-remains-and-god-machine#post26252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I have read in the previews, it looks like the upcoming book Hunter: Mortal Remains will also have the necessary information to pull a Hunter game into the post God Machine rules set.<br /> <br /> My question is, will the new material presented in this book be only compatible for Post GMC or will it be in the classic format and you use the rules to pull it into GMC. The reason I ask this question is that I am not a big fan of the GMC rules update and I would enjoy this book a lot more if I dont have to reverse engineer the new material to use it with my non-GMC WOD. The acronyms!!!<br /> <br /> Anyone have any incite to this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say two of the MANY Dread Powers reference Conditions. <br /> <br /> You could just completely ignore the update chapter whole-cloth. The organization Merits all reference Merits that exist in WoD core and HtV as well as GMC. <br /> <br /> So, tl;dr, you will be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T17:39:24-08:00","id":32864,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if the Promethean Chapter is going to deal with applying Disquiet to PCs (with NPCs its easy enough, but PCs gets into the whole &quot;don't tell me how to play my character!&quot; fights). Making it a Condition that is resolved (earning Beats) by acting against the Promethean would be a potentially elegant carrot-based solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T05:25:14-08:00","id":33086,"title":"","content":"One thing I sometimes have a bit of problem with is knowing which condition to apply in some situations. Like, old powers, for instance. Hope the Mortal Remains rules chapter tell us which Conditions to apply in some Endowments, including those from sourcebooks. Perhaps just a table, like: Mask of Terror - Now causes the Dread Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}